<title>ISRAEL: Israel government delays vote on savings tax.</title>
<headline>Israel government delays vote on savings tax.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's cabinet adopted on Monday a package of capital market reform measures, but delayed for two weeks a decision on taxing savings of less than 10 years' duration, a finance ministry spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;Senior officials on the level of directors-general from the Bank of Israel, the finance ministry, and the prime minister's office will continue to debate the savings tax issue for two weeks. Until then no tax will be implemented,&quot; the spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
</text>
